{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"446","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. DZY Loves Games"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Today DZY begins to play an old game. In this game, he is in a big maze with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" rooms connected by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" corridors (each corridor allows to move in both directions). You can assume that all the rooms are connected with corridors directly or indirectly."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"DZY has got lost in the maze. Currently he is in the first room and has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" lives. He will act like the follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Firstly he will randomly pick one of the corridors going from his current room. Each outgoing corridor has the same probability to be picked. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then he will go through the corridor and then the process repeats. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are some rooms which have traps in them. The first room definitely has no trap, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th room definitely has a trap. Each time DZY enters one of these rooms, he will lost one life. Now, DZY knows that if he enters the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th room with exactly 2 lives, firstly he will lost one live, but then he will open a bonus round. He wants to know the probability for him to open the bonus round. Please, help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m, k (2 ≤ n ≤ 500; 1 ≤ m ≤ 105; 2 ≤ k ≤ 109)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers, each of them is either "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th number is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th room has a trap, otherwise it has not a trap. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please note"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", that the number of rooms with a trap is no more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"101"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that the first room has no trap, and the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th room has a trap."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines follows. Each of them contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ui, vi (1 ≤ ui, vi ≤ n; ui ≠ vi)"},{"kind":"text","text":", meaning that current corridor connects two rooms "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ui"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"vi"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that the corridor system is connected."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the only real number — the probability for DZY to open the bonus round. The answer will be considered correct if its relative or absolute error doesn't exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 4"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 5 3\n0 0 1 0 1\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 5\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0.25000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 2 2\n0 1 1\n1 2\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-0.00000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1 3\n0 1\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1.00000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"446D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/446/problem/D"}